00:10:18.860 --> 00:10:19.360
Hello?

00:10:19.660 --> 00:10:20.160
Hi!

00:10:20.420 --> 00:10:22.340
Oh, I found the room of blood!

00:10:22.340 --> 00:10:23.320
Oh, good!

00:10:23.620 --> 00:10:24.340
Oh, great! Yay!

00:10:24.540 --> 00:10:26.140
Oh, jeez, what is this?!

00:10:26.900 --> 00:10:27.400
Oh.

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:27.980
Hi.

00:10:28.340 --> 00:10:29.220
How ya doing? (Not bad, you?)

00:10:29.400 --> 00:10:29.900
Ho-hoh.

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:31.280
Is this the happy room?

00:10:31.280 --> 00:10:33.540
Is that why there's so many smile- ohhh.

00:10:34.780 --> 00:10:35.280
Okay.

00:10:36.180 --> 00:10:37.480
Oh, I found something...

00:10:37.480 --> 00:10:37.980
Oof...

00:10:38.360 --> 00:10:39.000
Oooof.

00:10:39.000 --> 00:10:40.660
You do not look comfortable...

00:10:41.060 --> 00:10:42.420
Well, maybe there's- ummm...

00:10:43.160 --> 00:10:44.440
Some bad-a-wee's here...

00:10:44.440 --> 00:10:46.020
Okay, got some batteries!

00:10:46.020 --> 00:10:48.680
Very loud and startle-y bad-a-wee's, but I got it!

00:10:49.260 --> 00:10:49.800
Okay?

00:10:49.980 --> 00:10:54.460
Ahhh, come onnnn, you can't just give me the happy room.

00:10:55.200 --> 00:10:55.700
Eugh.

00:10:56.560 --> 00:10:58.400
So that thing IS out there.

00:10:59.820 --> 00:11:02.240
That is something we have readily deter-manned.

00:11:02.620 --> 00:11:07.480
And I have a feeling you're supposed to conserve your sprint juice so that you can go farther...

00:11:07.760 --> 00:11:09.120
When it's chasing you.

00:11:09.400 --> 00:11:10.680
And probably, uh...

00:11:11.360 --> 00:11:14.820
Flash the flashlight at it, and that's the thing that'll get ya safe.

00:11:15.500 --> 00:11:16.940
Okay, so *that's* bricked up.

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:19.620
But where the hell else am I suppose--

00:11:19.620 --> 00:11:22.140
Heeeeey, no! No! Begone, demon!

00:11:22.140 --> 00:11:25.440
Begoooooone demon! AHHHH!

00:11:25.440 --> 00:11:28.300
I'm fuuuuuuuucked.

00:11:31.640 --> 00:11:32.200
I'm dead.

00:11:32.200 --> 00:11:35.260
Okay, so this seems a lot more complicated than

00:11:35.820 --> 00:11:37.860
I would assume it to be, and a lot more challenging

00:11:37.860 --> 00:11:40.300
Because, number one, you gotta manage your resources

00:11:40.300 --> 00:11:42.240
in terms of your flashlight battery,

00:11:42.240 --> 00:11:43.280
and number two,

00:11:43.620 --> 00:11:45.460
how can you avoid that thing

00:11:46.180 --> 00:11:49.220
if as soon as it sees you, it starts chasing you faster than you can sprint,

00:11:49.220 --> 00:11:50.920
and you can't sprint that long to begin with?

00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:51.780
Like, what are you even looking for?

00:11:51.780 --> 00:11:52.280
So,

00:11:52.820 --> 00:11:55.760
It's not very obvious, so if you want me to finish this, let me know what

00:11:55.760 --> 00:11:59.100
to do down in the comments below, I'll need your help with this one,

00:11:59.100 --> 00:12:01.500
and I'll probably need to look up a guide or something,

00:12:01.500 --> 00:12:05.760
but it seems to have potential, but it had m-more potential in the beginning

00:12:05.760 --> 00:12:08.680
than it did at the end, it was a more interesting game

00:12:08.680 --> 00:12:10.820
in those first few days than it was in the sewer.

00:12:10.820 --> 00:12:15.320
I will readily admit, like I'm not wanting to be too harsh on this, I'm just saying what it was.

00:12:15.320 --> 00:12:17.720
It really was interesting in those first few days.

00:12:17.720 --> 00:12:18.760
So, either way,

00:12:18.760 --> 00:12:20.300
Thank you everybody so much for watching

00:12:20.300 --> 00:12:22.620
Lemme know what you thought of this game down in the comments below,

00:12:22.620 --> 00:12:23.580
and as always,

00:12:23.800 --> 00:12:24.580
I will see you...

00:12:25.260 --> 00:12:26.280
In the next video.

00:12:26.920 --> 00:12:27.840
BUH-byeee!

